{
  "_comment": "Golden parity fixtures for routing chain intermediates into the run scratch: the plan rewrite that runs after the NL gates and before a skill's collision repair, for a skill whose skill.yaml sets `scratch_intermediates: true`. An intermediate is a step's `output` that a later step reads; it moves to `<work>/` keeping its place relative to the user's folder, and every later reference follows. An output nothing reads is a deliverable and stays; a file the user named in the request stays; with no utterance, every name is the caller's and nothing moves. Fixed plans in, the routed plan out, no model. `<work>` is the run's scratch folder and `<sandbox>` the folder paths resolve against; consumers substitute real directories and compare with `/` separators. Consumed by python/core/tests/test_scratch_routing_parity.py and native/crates/knaif-core/tests/scratch_routing_parity.rs. WHY: an intermediate left in the user's folder was one of the four leftover-file sources (36 ffmpeg rows, 129 files); both runtimes must move the same files to the same places, or the same utterance leaves different files behind.",
  "joining_tools": [
    "concat_video",
    "merge_pdfs"
  ],
  "_joining_tools": "Tools whose several inputs become ONE output (tools.yaml `joins_inputs: true`). A producer with a glob is never routed; one with several inputs is routed only when it joins them. Consumers pass this set.",
  "cases": [
    {
      "name": "an_unnamed_intermediate_moves_with_its_reader",
      "utterance": "trim clip.mp4 to 2 seconds, then resize it",
      "plan": [
        {
          "tool": "trim_video",
          "args": {
            "input": "clip.mp4",
            "end": "00:00:02",
            "output": "clip_trimmed.mp4"
          }
        },
        {
          "tool": "resize_video",
          "args": {
            "inputs": [
              "clip_trimmed.mp4"
            ],
            "height": 240
