      "name": "a_glob_producer_is_never_routed",
      "_why": "ffmpeg_134#2: a batch over `*` writes one file per input under the one `output` name; only one is read later, the rest are deliverables. Routing the step sent them all to the scratch, where they were deleted. Same rule as chain linking: one output cannot name a fan-out.",
      "utterance": "MP3 nach WAV konvertieren und Samplerate auf 22050 Hz setzen",
      "plan": [
        {
          "tool": "extract_audio",
          "args": {
            "inputs": [
              "*"
